  "title": "Caravaggio (Michelangelo Merisi)",
  "summary": "Michelangelo Merisi, called Caravaggio, was an Italian painter born in 1571 who moved to Rome in 1592. His first major commission was the St Matthew canvases for the Contarelli Chapel in San Luigi dei Francesi. After killing a man in a duel in 1606 he fled south, and he died at Porto Ercole on 18 July 1610.",
